  "title": "A Pollinations workspace in Open WebUI",
  "summary": "A compact shipping sprint broadened the ways builders can chat, generate, connect agents, and keep working when providers get temperamental.\n\nOpen WebUI launched with Pollinations login, the full text-model picker, and MCP-powered image, video, and audio tools inside conversations. Managed-agent calls also render cleanly across streamed and standard chats.\n\nThe catalog grew with Gemini 3.8 Flash, Qwen3.8 Max 0902, Mercury 2.5 Preview, DeepSeek V4 Flash Vision, Claude Fable 5.1, and expanded Wan video workflows including reference, audio, and end-frame generation.\n\nA stateless OpenAI-compatible Responses API arrived across 56 direct-provider models, while Composio connectors let agents work through caller-owned app accounts. Hosted MCP gained canonical guides, architecture documentation, source links, and more reliable generation handling.\n\nSearch, filters, model metadata, agent capabilities, and MCP cards became easier to inspect, while verified fallback routes and clearer response headers helped requests keep their public model identity when upstreams needed a moment.",
